UID:ars-electronica-u19-create-your-world-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150945Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270303
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270304
SUMMARY:Deadline: Prix Ars Electronica: u19 create your world 2027 (Austria
 \, under 20)
DESCRIPTION:u19 create your world is the youth category of the Prix Ars Ele
 ctronica\, for young people in Austria working with digital media\, techno
 logy\, games\, code\, film\, music\, art and design. Individuals\, project
  groups and school projects may enter.\n\nOrganisation: Ars Electronica (P
 rix Ars Electronica)\nLocation: Linz\, Austria\; open only to people aged 
 19 or younger who live in Austria on 3 March 2027\nAward: Young Profession
 als (14 to 19): Golden Nica EUR 3\,000\, two Awards of Distinction EUR 800
  each\, ten Honorary Mentions. Young Creatives (up to 14): per age group (
 u10\, u12\, u14) one EUR 500 Prize plus an Award of Distinction (EUR 150 f
 or u14\, EUR 100 for u12 and u10). No entry fee mentioned.\nDuration: One-
 off prize\n\nMore: https://ars.electronica.art/createyourworld/en/prix/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ars.electronica.art/createyourworld/en/prix/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Linz\, Austria\; open only to people aged 19 or younger who live i
 n Austria on 3 March 2027
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ecf-erasmus-40-creative-research-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150945Z
DTSTART:20261201T153000Z
DTEND:20261201T160000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 CET: European Cultural Foundation: ERASMUS 40 Creati
 ve Research Fellowship (Florence archives\, Brussels presentation)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 17:00 CET.\n\nTo mark the 40th anniversar
 y of ERASMUS in 2027\, the European Cultural Foundation is opening its his
 torical archives for a Creative Research Fellowship: one professional crea
 tive practitioner will research ECF's lesser-known role in shaping the ERA
 SMUS student mobility programme (from the European Institute of Education 
 and the Office for Cooperation in Education to the ERASMUS Bureau\, which 
 ran...\n\nOrganisation: European Cultural Foundation (ECF)\, with the Hist
 orical Archives of the European Union (EUI) and the House of European Hist
 ory\nLocation: Research stay in Florence\, Italy (Historical Archives of t
 he EU) in the first trimester of 2027\; final work presented in Brussels i
 n September 2027. Open to creative practitioners residing in a Council of 
 Europe member state.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 grant covering travel\, living ex
 penses and artistic production. One fellowship.\nDuration: Research reside
 ncy in Florence in the first trimester of 2027 (January to March)\; presen
 tation in September 2027\n\nMore: https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Research stay in Florence\, Italy (Historical Archives of the EU) 
 in the first trimester of 2027\; final work presented in Brussels in Septe
 mber 2027. Open to creative practitioners residing in a Council of Europe 
 member state.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai-horizons-parma-360-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150945Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI Horizons: Art Beyond Algorithms (PARMA 360 Festival\, 
 Parma European Youth Capital 2027)
DESCRIPTION:First edition of an international call for artists under 35 wor
 king with artificial intelligence\, digital languages and emerging technol
 ogies\, run by 360° Creativity Events APS for PARMA 360 Festival and Parm
 a European Youth Capital 2027. It follows the 2026 pilot exhibition SYNTHE
 TIC HORIZONS (curated by Chiara Canali).\n\nOrganisation: 360° Creativity
  Events APS (PARMA 360 Festival della creatività contemporanea)\, with Pa
 rma European Youth Capital 2027\nLocation: Parma\, Italy. Open to Italian 
 and international artists under 35 and students of the Accademie di Belle 
 Arti. Finalists exhibit in Parma in April-May 2027.\nAward: EUR 6\,000 in 
 cash prizes (gross): 1st AI Horizons Prize EUR 1\,500 (overall winner) plu
 s three sponsor prizes of EUR 1\,500 each (Polo Parma for Parma Heritage\,
  COLSER-Auroradomus for La Cura\, DS Solutions for Sustainability and Data
  Ecology). The top prize can be combined with a sponsor prize\, so one art
 ist can receive up to EUR 3\,000. Prizes are treated as full or partial ac
 quisition of the work. Non-cash: Piazza of Beauty residency in Parma durin
 g the show\, plus Rome New Media Week 2027 and Premio Giovanarte exhibitio
 n mentions. Free to enter.\nDuration: Finalist group exhibition in April-M
 ay 2027 (11th PARMA 360 Festival)\n\nMore: https://forms.gle/ymoWbcjuDyzJY
 11P6?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://forms.gle/ymoWbcjuDyzJY11P6?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Parma\, Italy. Open to Italian and international artists under 35 
 and students of the Accademie di Belle Arti. Finalists exhibit in Parma in
  April-May 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:athens-digital-arts-festival-2027-open-call@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150945Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Athens Digital Arts Festival 2027 (23rd edition): Open Ca
 ll "It's Alive..."
DESCRIPTION:The Athens Digital Arts Festival\, Greece's long-running digita
 l arts festival\, has opened its call for the 23rd edition in spring 2027 
 under the theme "It's Alive..." (Dr. Frankenstein's line\, reread for an a
 ge when we feel the same relief when the Wi-Fi comes back). CATEGORIES: Vi
 deo Art\, Installations\, Performances\, Animation\, Games\, Web Art\, AR/
 VR/XR\, Music\, Talks\, Workshops and ADAF Kids.\n\nOrganisation: Athens D
 igital Arts Festival (ADAF)\nLocation: Athens\, Greece (23rd edition\, spr
 ing 2027). Open to artists\, researchers\, thinkers and organisations worl
 dwide.\nAward: NO PUBLISHED CASH\, listed under the desk's festival except
 ion (festival calls with a firm deadline may be added without a cash amoun
 t). No entry fee. Postal submission costs and artwork transport are at the
  artist's expense unless agreed otherwise.\n\nMore: https://2027.adaf.gr/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://2027.adaf.gr/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
LOCATION:Athens\, Greece (23rd edition\, spring 2027). Open to artists\, re
 searchers\, thinkers and organisations worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:thessaloniki-documentary-festival-agora-xr-lab-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150945Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261126
SUMMARY:Deadline: Thessaloniki Documentary Festival: AGORA XR Lab 2027 (XR 
 and new media projects in development)
DESCRIPTION:A development lab for XR and new media projects at the Thessalo
 niki International Documentary Festival's industry section AGORA\, for eme
 rging storytellers working across film\, digital media\, new technologies 
 and performing arts. Lead mentor: Vassiliki Khonsari (co-founder\, iNK Sto
 ries). Up to five projects are selected.\n\nOrganisation: Thessaloniki Int
 ernational Documentary Festival (TIDF AGORA)\nLocation: Thessaloniki\, Gre
 ece (online workshop mid-January 2027\, in-person lab 6-11 March 2027). Ai
 med at projects produced or co-produced in\, or with story links to\, Sout
 heast and Central Europe\, the Mediterranean and parts of the Middle East 
 and North Africa\; projects from elsewhere may still apply.\nAward: NO CAS
 H\, listed under the desk's festival exception (festival calls with a firm
  deadline may be added without a cash amount). Selected projects get 5 nig
 hts' accommodation (one double room for two members)\, partial travel reim
 bursement against receipts\, mentoring and curated industry meetings. No a
 pplication fee stated.\nDuration: Online workshop mid-January 2027\, in-pe
 rson lab 6-11 March 2027\n\nMore: https://filmfestival.gr/en/tidf/tidf-ago
 ra/agora-xr-lab/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://filmfestival.gr/en/tidf/tidf-agora/agora-xr-lab/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Thessaloniki\, Greece (online workshop mid-January 2027\, in-perso
 n lab 6-11 March 2027). Aimed at projects produced or co-produced in\, or 
 with story links to\, Southeast and Central Europe\, the Mediterranean and
  parts of the Middle East and North Africa\; projects from elsewhere may s
 till apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:khk-cure-fellowships-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150945Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Deadline: KHK CURE Fellowships 2027/2028\, Saarland University (the
 me: Things)
DESCRIPTION:The Kaete Hamburger Centre for Cultural Practices of Reparation
  (KHK CURE) at Saarland University invites applications for up to twelve f
 ellowships for its fourth year\, October 2027 to September 2028.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Kaete Hamburger Centre for Cultural Practices of Reparation (CURE)
 \, Saarland University\nLocation: Saarbruecken\, Germany. Fellows must liv
 e in Saarbruecken during the fellowship and participate actively in centre
  events\; extended research absences are not permitted. Open international
 ly\; retired persons and Saarland University staff are not eligible.\nAwar
 d: Up to twelve fellowships. Fellows on unpaid leave from their institutio
 n receive approximately EUR 6\,100 to 7\,200 per month before taxes\, depe
 nding on qualifications\; alternatively\, fellows retaining their salary c
 an have their home institution reimbursed for replacement teaching. One ro
 und trip to Saarbruecken is reimbursed\, a fully equipped individual works
 pace is provided\, and an apartment can be arranged for around EUR 1\,250 
 per month. Eligible accompanying family members may receive additional sup
 port. No application fee.\nDuration: Six to twelve months\, beginning 1 Oc
 tober 2027\n\nMore: https://cure.uni-saarland.de/en/fellows/call-for-appli
 cations?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cure.uni-saarland.de/en/fellows/call-for-applications?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Saarbruecken\, Germany. Fellows must live in Saarbruecken during t
 he fellowship and participate actively in centre events\; extended researc
 h absences are not permitted. Open internationally\; retired persons and S
 aarland University staff are not eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150945Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) runs this r
 esidency with Videotage\, a Hong Kong-based non-profit media arts institut
 ion specialising in the promotion\, presentation\, creation and preservati
 on of moving image and media art in all forms and languages.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL) in
  collaboration with Videotage\, Hong Kong\nLocation: Residency takes place
  at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must be established in the Netherla
 nds\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (K
 ingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within th
 e Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 for a two-month residency
  or EUR 6\,500 for a three-month residency\, paid by the Creative Industri
 es Fund NL to cover travel\, insurance\, living expenses\, compensation fo
 r time invested\, and material and transport costs. Accommodation\, use of
  the studio space and facilitation by Videotage are covered directly by th
 e Fund on top of this. No application fee.\nDuration: Two or three months 
 in 2027 (spring 2027)\; state your preferred period in the application.\n\
 nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Videotage in Hong Kong. Applicants must b
 e established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint
  Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in 
 a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultuurloket-digitall-implementatiebijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150945Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cultuurloket DigitALL: Implementation Contribution (Imple
 mentatiebijdrage\, 2026)
DESCRIPTION:A one-off 2026 call letting Dutch cultural institutions reuse a
 nd adapt digital technology that other institutions have already built and
  published in the open DigitALL Toolkit\, for example translation software
  shared between theatres or a streaming platform adapted for a new venue. 
 Grants run up to EUR 30\,000 and cover technical modification\, integratio
 n\, production and deployment costs.\n\nOrganisation: Cultuurloket DigitAL
 L\nLocation: Netherlands and the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom. No city o
 r region restriction.\nAward: Up to EUR 30\,000. Covers technical modifica
 tion\, system integration\, production and deployment costs. Hardware purc
 hase alone is ineligible unless clearly essential to the public experience
 . No stated co-financing percentage. No application fee.\nDuration: Not sp
 ecified\; scoped to a single implementation.\n\nMore: https://cultuurloket
 digitall.nl/implementatiebijdrage/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://cultuurloketdigitall.nl/implementatiebijdrage/?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands and the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom. No city or reg
 ion restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:foresight-ai-science-safety-nodes-grants@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T150945Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Foresight Institute: AI for Science & Safety Nodes RFP
DESCRIPTION:Umbrella request for proposals for ambitious AI-first projects 
 that make the transition to capable AI go well and use it to unlock scienc
 e. Three connected layers\, each with its own detailed call: I. Local Comp
 ute (compute that individuals or communities physically own and control)\;
  II.\n\nOrganisation: Foresight Institute\nLocation: Remote (global\; hubs
  in San Francisco and Berlin)\nAward: Typically $30\,000 to $100\,000 per 
 grant\, with smaller amounts for the Human Empowerment and AI Insurance & 
 Open Governance focus areas and higher amounts for the rest (larger possib
 le for the right project)\, plus private local compute and workspace at th
 e San Francisco or Berlin AI Nodes. No application fee.\nDuration: Project
 -based\n\nMore: https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote (global\; hubs in San Francisco and Berlin)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
